[Music]  foreign  looking to get a better understanding of  how your trained models are making  decisions with the help of vertex  explainable AI you can better understand  explain and interpret your model's  outputs and predictions hi I'm Chloe  Condon a developer advocate for Google  cloud and in this video I'm going to  give you an overview of vertex Ai and  show you how vertex explainable AI can  help you better understand your model's  outputs for classification and  regression tasks let's get started  to better understand vertex explainable  AI let's quickly cover what vertex AI is  and how it works  vertex AI is Google Cloud's end-to-end  machine learning platform that helps  engineers and data scientists accelerate  machine learning experimentation and  deployment  it brings together Google Cloud's  existing ml offerings into a single  environment for efficiently building and  managing the life cycle of ml projects  in one single place you can import and  label your data and train evaluate and  deploy your model once the model is  deployed vertex AI allows you to get  your predictions using either command  line interface console AI or the SDK or  apis  explainable AI comes into play in the  model training and evaluation steps of  the process  when assessing explanations we want to  know what factors play a role in  defining the predictions that have been  provided that's where example-based  explanations and feature attributions  come into play  let's take for example a machine  learning model that predicts whether a  coffee shop is open or not with feature  attributions you could get an  explanation like the coffee shop is not  open because the door is locked in this  scenario the coffee shop is a feature  and the closed door is an attribute of  that feature with explainable AI example  based or similarity explanations provide  us with more context and secondary  information to help explain and  emphasize the differences in our data  and explain how the model Acts  for example here are 10 other coffee  shops that are closed and the doors are  also locked  this includes more context and secondary  information for us to better understand  differences in our data set and or how  the model is acting since vertex AI is  able to tell us how much each feature  contributed to the predicted result with  feature attribution as well as find  similar examples from example based we  can then use this information to verify  that the model is behaving as expected  recognize bias in your models and get  ideas for how to improve your model and  training your data keep an eye out for  future videos where we dive deeper into  feature attribution and example-based  explanations  understanding how machine learning  models make predictions and being able  to communicate those insights to  external stakeholders and other people  within your organization is a key part  of being able to properly evaluate and  interpret your machine learning models  having clear and accurate explanations  for models can help several groups  within your organization be it your  model Builders data scientists and ml  Ops who want to better understand why  their model isn't performing or how to  improve it  end users of machine learning systems  are looking to see if they can trust the  model or make decisions on how to  respond to the prediction  or public stakeholders within or outside  your organization who may be involved in  regulatory or compliance with your  machine learning models  they can use explanations to make sure  models are safe to use and help develop  guidance for Industries on responsible  use of AI  the insights provided by vertex  explainable AI can be used to figure out  exactly why or how these models came to  specific conclusions and help you  evaluate your ml model's predictions  in this video we talked about vertex Ai  and how explainable AI provides us with  the tools needed to better interpret  your model's predictions in our next  video we'll dive a little deeper and go  over some examples of how you can use  custom Frameworks to analyze models in  the meantime if you'd like to get  started you can go to the explainable AI  documentation Linked In the description  or scan the QR code on the screen for  more information and step-by-step guides  thanks for tuning in  [Music]

